==English==

===Etymology===

{{suffix|authentic|ity}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|authenticities}}

# The quality of being [[genuine]] or not corrupted from the original.
#: ''I hereby certify that this is an '''authentic''' copy.''
# Truthfulness of origins, attributions, commitments, sincerity, and intentions.
#: ''The painting was not '''authentic''' after all; it was just a copy.''
# {{obsolete}} The quality of being [[authentic]] (of established [[authority]]).

====Synonyms====
*{{sense|quality of being genuine}} [[genuineness]]

====Antonyms====
*{{sense|quality of not being genuine}} [[phoniness]]; [[forgery]]; [[fakeness]]; [[bogosity]]

====Related terms====
*[[authentically]]

